 "polityNote": "Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal, the seven provinces of the 2015 constitution (before 20 September 2015 the zones are drawn by NPL.json from Natural Earth). Atoms: geoBoundaries ADM3 of NPL (2019 gaunpalikas and nagarpalikas with national parks and reserves, Open Data Nepal / MoFAGA, CC BY-SA 4.0). A province is the union of the local units whose majority lies in it on the Survey Department’s province map (geoBoundaries ADM1, OCHA, a different publisher); the local units of 2017 were formed inside the 77 districts, which carry the Schedule 4 lines including the Nawalparasi and Rukum splits. ① Union area against the Survey Department province polygons: Province 1 26,111/26,105 km², Province 2 9,610/9,607, Bagmati 20,334/20,329, Gandaki 22,014/22,009, Lumbini 19,269/19,292, Karnali 30,793/30,759, Sudurpashchim 19,774/19,769 (with Byas) — all within 0.12%.",
